00:01:09.388 --> 00:01:11.430
customer who built their
marketing data warehouse

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.850
with Google Cloud Platform.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.080
Today we want to showcase
how quick and easy

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.750
it is to build a marketing data
warehouse using Google Cloud

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:22.520
Platform to drive your
marketing analytics initiatives.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.400
With that, let's get started.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.250
Marketing data warehouses are
becoming a critical component

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.590
of enterprises to accelerate
their marketing analytics

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.700
initiatives.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.810
Customer journeys
have many touchpoints.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.840
A known customer or
an unknown visitor,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.840
they're all generating
data through interactions

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:43.490
across channels and devices like
email, websites, applications,

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.410
point of sale, et cetera.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.360
These touchpoints are
generating more data

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.380
than businesses
can make sense of.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.650
For instance, visitors are
generating web traffic data

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.300
while ad exposure
data is collected

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.790
across multiple
advertising systems.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.190
CRM and sales data is collected
across multiple systems

00:01:58.190 --> 00:01:59.180
as well.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.460
Having a consolidated
and holistic view

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.670
of all of the data is key to
delivering enhanced customer

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:05.670
experience.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.460
This requires organizing
and leveraging

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.340
all the data enterprises
have about customers

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.230
across touchpoints.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.910
Enterprises do
recognize the value

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.060
of building a comprehensive
marketing data

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:19.782
warehouse to solve their
critical business needs.

00:02:19.782 --> 00:02:21.240
So let's look at
the business needs

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.150
that enterprises are trying to
address with marketing and data

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.230
warehouse.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.320
First and foremost
is Customer 360.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.690
Enterprises are seeking
to build Customer 360,

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.420
a source-of-truth
record to tie all,

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.360
or almost all, of touchpoints
together to fully understand

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.430
customer journey,
behaviors, and preferences.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.380
One key challenge is data silos.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:44.820
Enterprises have data silos in
multiple databases and systems.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:48.560
All these systems and databases
are collecting diverse data

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.820
around customers and visitors.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.520
All of this data needs to be
brought into a single data

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.650
warehouse to transform
before it can be made part

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.020
of a single Customer
360 [? deployment, ?]

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.360
capturing as much
information as possible

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.560
around the customer
and its visitors.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.450
The second key point
is personalization,

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.370
or the business need
is personalization,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.770
making the marketing data
warehouses enable greater

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.240
level of personalization.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.980
A stronger understanding
of the customer

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.720
through full view of
all the touchpoints

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.060
provide greater
capability to personalize

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.060
customers' experiences
such as shopping, browsing,

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.860
email marketing, et cetera.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:24.070
Consolidated data also
provides visibility

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.630
into customer preferences,
allowing enterprises

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:30.300
to personalize with higher
accuracy and greater results.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.840
The third key business
need is around measurement.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.603
Enterprises are leveraging
multiple Software as a Service,

00:03:35.603 --> 00:03:38.270
or SaaS, backbones for executing
their marketing and advertising

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.460
campaigns, such as email,
display ads, searches, videos,

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.470
et cetera.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.860
All of these campaigns
generate data on ad exposure.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.510
Collecting campaign
performance data

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:50.210
and feeding it back into
marketing data warehouse

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.180
allows enterprises to understand
the campaign performance

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.520
and [INAUDIBLE] optimize
marketing and advertising

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.100
campaigns.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.690
The fourth business
need is around security.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:02.330
Marketing data
warehouses are used

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.300
not just to ingest data from
third-party data providers,

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.120
but also to share data
back with these providers.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.870
Security is a key need for
building marketing data

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:14.120
warehouse since customers and
visitor data, which sometimes

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.180
is Personally Identifiable
Information, or PII,

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.310
is shared between
systems and platforms.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.800
Data ingestion and export
to third-party systems

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.480
should be highly
secure, as customers

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.480
have trusted enterprises
with storing and keeping

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.850
their data safe.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.692
And the final business need
is around machine learning.

00:04:31.692 --> 00:04:33.150
Marketing data
warehouses should be

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.400
able to connect to and leverage
machine learning products

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.817
to build scalable
machine learning

00:04:36.817 --> 00:04:38.700
products such as
customer segmentation,

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.117
lifetime value of the customer,
purchase [? aspiration, ?]

00:04:41.117 --> 00:04:41.790
et cetera.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.060
Customer 360 data in
marketing data warehouses

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.700
will allow data engineering
and data scientists

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.450
to come together to
build machine learning

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.150
models for marketers that
can be used for activation

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.260
across multiple platforms.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.140
So now we have seen
that enterprises

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.150
do have a clear need for
building marketing data

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:57.960
warehouses.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.870
They quickly encounter a
number of technology challenges

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.970
that hamper their
ability to move quickly

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:05.060
and achieve these
outlined business needs.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.720
Enterprises run into these
four key technology challenges

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.290
while building a marketing
data warehouse-- data silos,

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.540
software as a service
platforms integration,

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.820
data integration
needs, and activation.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.900
Let's look at each of these
challenges one by one.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.970
Speaking of data silos,
data is fragmented

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.670
across multiple databases.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:29.130
Certain data sets are housed
on-prem across databases

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:31.810
and have existing connections
to bring the data in.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:35.230
Data is also shared through
a different mechanism.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.190
For instance, your vendor
might be providing data access

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.620
through API, or landing
that data on an FTP server

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.900
for you to pick up on
a regular schedule.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.390
Data velocity also differs
across enterprises.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.330
CRM and sales data might
be coming in as batch,

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:51.535
whereas website visits might
be coming in in near real time

00:05:51.535 --> 00:05:53.343
or real time.

00:05:53.343 --> 00:05:55.510
Finally, enterprises also
use multi-cloud strategies

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:58.370
so certain data sets might
be available on other public

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:01.590
clouds or on-prem systems.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.880
The second technology challenge
is software as a service

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.470
platforms integration.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.930
Enterprises leverage a number
of marketing and advertising

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.560
platforms to set up and
execute data campaigns.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.810
All of these Software as a
Service, or SaaS, platforms

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:14.720
provide data.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.110
Ingesting and integrating data
from these multiple platforms

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.570
become a huge challenge
since enterprises

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.190
have to set up
siloed integration

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.580
points to get these data sets
into marketing data warehouse.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.400
Managing and maintaining
these silos' integrations

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.980
is also a major challenge
for enterprises.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:34.800
The third technology challenge
is around data integration.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:37.140
Once the data from diverse
systems, databases,

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.870
and platforms have landed,
there are clear requirements

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:40.860
for data integration.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.710
Data needs to be
wrangled and transformed

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.940
with sophisticated
data pipelines.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.610
This step is also critical for
building Customer 360, where

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:52.040
enterprises are looking to join
multiple and diverse data sets

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.790
around customer touchpoints.

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.890
Another example would be
that consolidated data

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.120
needs to be aggregated
for marketer and executive

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:59.430
reporting.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.220
Finally, data can be
prepared using branding

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.810
and transformation
techniques to make

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.000
it easy for data science
activities such as model

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.250
development and deployment.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.980
And the fourth technology
challenge that we see

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.640
is around activation.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.160
Data in marketing
data warehouses

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.540
is used for marketing
analytics initiatives

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.500
such as segmentation, campaign
reporting, customer modeling,

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.320
et cetera.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:24.720
And these segments need to be
pushed back into SaaS platforms

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.490
for creating and
executing campaigns,

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.460
leveraging the insights for
marketing data warehouse.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.740
Similarly, raw data is
shared with partners

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.130
through multiple ways like SFTP.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:36.960
All of these
technology challenges

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:38.670
make it extremely
hard to deliver

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:42.990
marketing data warehouse vision
and its benefit to marketers.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.740
In the next section,
we'll learn about how

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.470
Cloud Data Fusion, along with
the Google Cloud Platform

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:50.140
products, provide
critical capabilities that

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.480
has enabled customers to
build their marketing data

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.455
warehouses.

00:07:54.455 --> 00:07:57.080
For this section, I will invite
Bhooshan Mogal, Product Manager

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.510
Cloud Data Fusion, to
take us through Cloud Data

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:03.660
Fusion and its capabilities
for marketing data warehouse.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.230
BHOOSHAN MOGAL: Thanks, Prateek.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:09.120
Let's get right into it and look
at how Cloud Data Fusion can

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.950
help you address some
of these business

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:14.630
needs and technical challenges,
like Prateek just spoke about,

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:17.520
and help you build out
your own marketing data

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.086
warehouse quickly and easily
on Google Cloud Platform.

00:08:22.086 --> 00:08:25.740
To get started, Data Fusion is
a cloud-native enterprise data

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:28.110
integration service
on Google Cloud.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.680
It provides you an end-to-end
data integration experience

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:34.650
that allows you to ingest,
prepare, transform, blend,

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:37.049
and enrich data from
various sources.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.990
It helps you build out
ETL and ELT pipelines

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.100
to curate data links
and data warehouses

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:46.290
on Google Cloud using a
simple point-and-click UI.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:50.160
Using this, you can then
focus on your business needs,

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.400
your business logic, and
build out your pipelines

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.650
without having to worry
about the intricacies

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:59.260
of infrastructure
and integration.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.750
This data shows you an overview
of Data Fusion's capabilities.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:05.240
With Data Fusion,
you can load data

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:07.370
by connecting to
disparate data sources

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.865
such as relational
databases, file

00:09:09.865 --> 00:09:13.130
based systems, modern
real-time messaging systems,

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:16.650
public cloud services, as
well as SaaS applications.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:18.350
It provides you a
development studio

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.240
in which you can drag
and drop sources,

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.930
transformations, and sinks to
develop your data pipelines.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:27.800
It also includes capabilities to
test, deploy, run, and monitor

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.870
pipelines, as well as provides
security and governance

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:34.120
controls for all data that
gets processed along the way.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:37.250
Data Fusion is built using
an open-source project called

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.600
CDAP.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.370
CDAP is an extensible
data application framework

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.700
which exposes high-level
business abstractions

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:46.490
and APIs over
complex technology,

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:51.200
using which developers can
build data applications easy.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:53.150
All around the world
taking advantage

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:57.810
of the latest and greatest
of cloud infrastructure.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:00.170
CDAP then takes care of
translating and executing

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:02.300
these applications
which you have

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:04.730
created using your
business logic

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:07.010
onto physical infrastructure.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:11.270
It consists of a core API and
a [? runtime. ?] Data Fusion

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:14.660
is built as an application
of the CDAP API

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:16.860
for data integration use cases.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.890
Data Fusion exposes
the wide experiences

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:22.640
for ingesting, wrangling,
integrating, and replicating

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:27.530
data to end users,
while hiding the details

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:31.250
of runtime and execution
environments from them.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:34.640
Additionally, it also
contains specific experiences

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:37.310
for industry verticals
such as healthcare,

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:40.700
which contain common
data integration patterns

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:44.630
within specific industries.

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:46.850
Users build out their
data integration pipelines

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:48.650
using these experiences.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.190
And then they can, in
turn, rely upon Data Fusion

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.570
to figure out the best
possible way to execute them

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:57.400
on physical infrastructure
on Google Cloud, and others,

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:00.080
without having to worry
about how that underlying

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.620
infrastructure works.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.440
The key value
proposition here is

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:06.620
that there is a separation
of design and runtime, which

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:10.520
allows you to build once
and execute anywhere.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.550
Currently, Data Fusion executes
pipelines as MapReduce or Spark

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.890
programs on Cloud Dataproc.

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:18.500
More execution engines such
as [? DataBlock, ?] Dataflow,

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:20.840
and BigQuery are on the roadmap.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.500
However, one of the key
aspects of Data Fusion's vision

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:27.860
is to abstract these execution
engines away from the user

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:31.170
and instead provide an
adaptive execution layer.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:33.860
This layer will then decide
the appropriate execution

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.470
environment to be used
for a pipeline based

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:39.920
on inputs such as SLA
and cost that users

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.350
can provide [INAUDIBLE].

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:47.492
Last, but not the least,
like we discussed,

00:11:47.492 --> 00:11:49.700
all the processing goes
through a standard processing

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:50.870
framework.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:55.190
Data Fusion can provide platform
capabilities such as security

00:11:55.190 --> 00:12:00.223
through IAM integration, private
access [INAUDIBLE],, et cetera,

00:12:00.223 --> 00:12:02.390
as well as metadata handling
the [INAUDIBLE] for all

